{% if androidVersions is not defined and android_versions is defined %}
  {% set androidVersions = android_versions %}
{% endif %}

<p>The below provides a table of Android versions and their respective API levels, release dates, estimated OS support end dates, and Google Play services cutoffs where documented.</p>
<p>Android versions are typically supported for an average of 3 years after their initial release, though this can vary based on manufacturer and device. </p>
<div class="callout">
  <strong>End of support (EOS)</strong> means Google has stopped backporting Android security fixes for that release. The OS support dates below are estimates, and device manufacturers may continue providing updates beyond them. <strong>End of life (EOL)</strong> means <a href="https://support.google.com/googleplay/answer/9037938?hl=en-GB">Google Play services</a> no longer receives updates on that Android version. Play services dates use the first day of the documented month because an exact last-update day is not available for every release. Day <code>01</code> is a placeholder. The month may mark Google's announcement, planned cutoff, or confirmation that support had ended. Sources are listed below the table.</div>
<p>Looking for minimum <code>targetSdkVersion</code> requirements? See the <a href="/android/android-minimum-targetsdk-matrix/">Android minimum target SDK matrix</a>.</p>
<p>There's a stable API for this table provided as JSON <a href="/api/android_versions.json">here</a>. The optional <code>playServicesEnd</code> field uses <code>YYYY-MM-01</code>, with day <code>01</code> standing for a documented month.</p>
<small>Last updated: {{ androidVersions.lastReviewed }}</small>

<div class="responsive-table-wrapper">
  <table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
    <th aria-label="Android icon">Icon</th>
    <th>Version</th>
    <th>Codename</th>
    <th>API version</th>
    <th>Release date</th>
    <th>Status</th>
    <th>OS support ended</th>
    <th>Play services cutoff</th>
    <th>Minor versions</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for item in androidVersions.items %}
    <tr>
      <td>
        {% if item.icon %}
          <img src="{{ item.icon }}" alt="Android {{ item.version }} icon" width="36" height="36" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        {% else %}
          -
        {% endif %}
      </td>
      <td>{{ item.version }}</td>
      <td>{{ item.codename }}</td>
      <td>{{ item.apiLevel }}</td>
      <td>{{ item.releaseDate }}</td>
      <td>
        {% set s = (item.status or '') | lower %}
        {% if s == 'maintained' %}
          {{ item.status | capitalize }}
        {% elif s in ['end-of-life','eol','end of life'] %}
          <span class="text-red">{{ item.status | capitalize }}</span>
        {% elif s == 'latest' %}
          <span class="text-green">{{ item.status | capitalize }}</span>
        {% elif item.status %}
          {{ item.status | capitalize }}
        {% else %}
          -
        {% endif %}
      </td>
      <td>
        {% if item.eolDate %}
          {{ item.eolDate }}
        {% else %}
          -
        {% endif %}
      </td>
      <td>
        {% if item.playServicesEnd %}
          <time datetime="{{ item.playServicesEnd }}">{{ item.playServicesEnd }}</time>
        {% else %}
          -
        {% endif %}
      </td>
      <td>
        {% if item.minorVersions %}
          {{ item.minorVersions | join(", ") }}
        {% else %}
          -
        {% endif %}
      </td>
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<p>Google Play services cutoff sources: <a href="https://android-developers.googleblog.com/2018/12/google-play-services-discontinuing.html">Android 4.0</a>, <a href="https://android-developers.googleblog.com/2021/07/google-play-services-discontinuing-jelly-bean.html">Android 4.1 to 4.3</a>, <a href="https://android-developers.googleblog.com/2023/07/google-play-services-discontinuing-updates-for-kitkat.html">Android 4.4</a>, <a href="https://9to5google.com/2024/07/11/android-lollipop-google-play-services/">Android 5</a>, and <a href="https://developers.google.com/android/management/release-notes">Android 6</a>.</p>

<p>Data sourced from <a href="https://developer.android.com/about/versions" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Android Developers</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Android_version_history" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikipedia (Android version history)</a>, and other public resources.</p>
